		Bestiary: {
			StinkFlyCritterBestiary: Flies that make themselves at home in the warm, nutrition-rich environment of the Crimson-infested underworld.
			PusSlugCritterBestiary: Slow and dumb, these slugs defend themselves by secreting acidic mucus... stay away!
			CursedCanariCritterBestiary: Lower concentrations of Imputed Flame can sometimes manifest as these harmless critters. Cute, but mind the heat!
			LavaLizardCritterBestiary: Juvenile form of the elusive Helldrake, these can be found scurrying around for food. Once grown, they fly off and are never seen again.
			CursedSpiritNPCBestiary: The power of the Corruption is such that even the inanimate can be made to do its bidding.
			CursehoundNPCBestiary: Cursed Spirits that accumulate too much power develop an armored form, and a monstrous ride to boot.
			DevilOWarNPCBestiary: Marine life in the underworld??? This organism uses hot gases to float in the air, and a sharp stinger to feed off its prey!
			EffigyNPCBestiary: Poor souls, overcome by the Corruption. Their twisted bodies now serve as cancerous hives, through which the darkness further spreads.
			TerrorBatNPCBestiary: These beasts stalk the cave ceilings in droves... the last thing you want to happen is to have your clothes stained by their acidic spit!
			ThoughtfulCultistNPCBesitary: Thirsting for power, these hell-born cultists have given themselves over to the Crimson entirely.
			CultistEyeBestiary: Somehow, the Crimson's cultists have learnt to wield Cthulhu's minions as their own...
			LanternBatNPCBestiary: Some servants of the Crimson occult have had their mind and bodies warped, forced to serve their masters as Lantern Bats.
			MarrowEyeNPCBestiary: Failed attempts at creating artificial Crimson Altars have resulted in the formation of these grotesque amalgmations of energy-infused flesh.
			PusImpNPCBestiary: An unholy mixture of Crimson bile and hell energy, these hollow imitations of hell's denizens only serve as extensions of the Crimson's will.
			StinkgrubNPCBestiary: Simple cavedwellers, engorged by the Crimson. These hardy grubs often migrate deeper underground in search of nutrients.
		}

